{"stories": [{"title": "Generate Formative Assessment Question Banks with Difficulty Levels", "priority": "high", "description": "Create Python script that generates reusable question collections for formative assessment (practice/self-test) for each CoCu. Questions should have difficulty levels (1-3) and be mapped to learning outcomes for student self-assessment and skill practice.", "acceptanceCriteria": ["scripts/generate_question_banks.py creates output/IT-020-{3,4,5}/formative_questions.json with 5-10 questions per work activity, each with difficulty level, Bloom's taxonomy classification, and learning outcome reference", "Question generator CLI: `uv run scripts/generate_question_banks.py --level 3 --format json` produces valid JSON with schema: {workActivity, questions: [{text, difficulty: 1-3, bloomLevel: string, learningOutcomeId: string}]}", "Generates minimum 100+ questions across all 20 CoCu files with balanced distribution: 40% Recall/Understand, 40% Apply/Analyze, 20% Evaluate/Create levels"], "estimatedComplexity": "medium"}, {"title": "Generate Instructor Facilitation Guides for Each CoCu", "priority": "high", "description": "Create Python script to generate comprehensive instructor guides for each CoCu including delivery strategies, time management, common student misconceptions, support materials, and assessment implementation guidance for teaching teams.", "acceptanceCriteria": ["scripts/generate_instructor_guides.py produces output/NOSS-IT-020-{3,4,5}-Instructor-Guides.docx with sections per CoCu: Overview, Learning Outcomes, Delivery Strategies, Time Allocation per Activity (minutes), Common Misconceptions, Troubleshooting Tips, Extension Activities, Assessment How-To", "Each guide includes: estimated teaching minutes per work activity, suggested teaching resources, differentiation strategies for diverse learners, connection between formative questions and summative assessment", "Guides integrate with CoCu markdown content to auto-pull work activities, learning outcomes, contact hours, and assessment criteria definitions"], "estimatedComplexity": "medium"}, {"title": "Create Student Competency Evidence Collection Framework", "priority": "high", "description": "Generate structured evidence collection templates and checklists that guide students on what evidence demonstrates competency for each work activity, aligned to 4-point competency rubrics and assessor expectations.", "acceptanceCriteria": ["scripts/generate_student_evidence_templates.py produces output/NOSS-IT-020-{3,4,5}-Evidence-Collection-Worksheets.docx with 1-2 evidence templates per work activity (40+ templates total)", "Each template includes: competency statement, evidence types accepted (written observation, practical demonstration, digital artifact, test score), reflection prompts, self-assessment rubric aligned to (Novice/Developing/Proficient/Advanced), assessor sign-off section", "Templates use clear student-facing language (grade 10-11 reading level, confirmed via Flesch-Kincaid index in validation script) with visual formatting and worked examples"], "estimatedComplexity": "medium"}, {"title": "Disability Accessibility Compliance Audit Script", "priority": "medium", "description": "Create Python script to automatically audit all 20 CoCu markdown source files and generated DOCX outputs against NOSS accessibility standards: readable font sizes/weights, alt text on all images, clear language standards (grade level), and sufficient color contrast.", "acceptanceCriteria": ["scripts/audit_accessibility.py scans content/IT-020-{3,4,5}/*.md and output/*.docx, generates output/Accessibility-Audit-Report.html with color-coded status per file: font readability (≥11pt pass), alt text coverage (≥95% pass), Flesch-Kincaid grade level (≤11th pass), WCAG color contrast (≥4.5:1 pass)", "Script categorizes issues as: Critical (blocks access), Major (impairs access), Minor (improvement suggested) and provides remediation guidance with examples", "Exit code: 0 if overall compliance ≥95%, 1 if <95%; audit counts files passing/failing per dimension and identifies patterns (e.g., 'Figures 1-12 missing alt text in CoCu-3')"], "estimatedComplexity": "medium"}, {"title": "Generate Work Activity Equivalencing Matrix Across Certification Levels", "priority": "medium", "description": "Create mapping document showing how each work activity at L3 (foundational skills) extends and specializes into L4 (intermediate specialization) and L5 (management/supervisory application), demonstrating pedagogical scaffolding across certification pathway.", "acceptanceCriteria": ["scripts/generate_level_equivalencing_matrix.py extracts work activities from all 20 CoCu files, produces output/Work-Activity-Equivalencing-Matrix.xlsx with columns: L3 Foundation Activity, L4 Specialized Application, L5 Management/Supervisory Application, Bloom Level Progression, Shared Competencies, Specialized Skills, Assessment Alignment", "Matrix maps 60+ core work activities with progressions (e.g., 'Troubleshoot hardware' L3 → 'Diagnose server hardware faults' L4 → 'Design hardware upgrade strategy' L5) and highlights any activities missing from progression chain", "Includes visual formatting with color gradient showing Bloom level progression and identifies which progression gaps require new activities"], "estimatedComplexity": "medium"}, {"title": "Validate Assessment Difficulty Progression Within Each CoCu", "priority": "medium", "description": "Create validator script that analyzes question/activity difficulty distribution and cognitive complexity within each CoCu to ensure scaffolded learning (easy→medium→hard) and balance between recall/application/analysis cognitive loads.", "acceptanceCriteria": ["scripts/validate_difficulty_progression.py reads formative_questions.json for each CoCu, produces output/Difficulty-Progression-Report.json with per-CoCu stats: difficulty distribution (%), Bloom level ladder check, cognitive balance score (0-100), and flagged issues", "Validator detects problems: unbalanced difficulty (one level >50%), cognitive jumps (Recall directly to Analyze with no Apply step), insufficient scaffolding (new concept introduced at hard level only)", "Report includes actionable recommendations: 'Add 3 medium-difficulty Apply questions to CoCu-2' or 'Split 1 hard question into Apply + Analyze progression' with example rewrites"], "estimatedComplexity": "small"}, {"title": "Generate Pre/Post Assessment Instruments for Learning Gain Measurement", "priority": "medium", "description": "Create standardized entry and exit assessment instruments for each CoCu to measure student learning gains from pre (prior knowledge baseline) to post (competency achievement). Pre identifies gaps; post certifies competency.", "acceptanceCriteria": ["scripts/generate_pre_post_assessments.py produces output/NOSS-IT-020-{3,4,5}-Pre-Post-Assessment-Suite.docx with paired pre/post assessments for all 20 CoCu files (40 instruments total, 8-10 questions each, ≤30 min each)", "Each assessment pair: pre-assessment uses different question stems/scenarios from post to prevent test-retest bias, both target identical learning outcomes, includes rubric and interpretation guide (≥70% = competent per NOSS standard)", "Includes: answer key, scoring rubric, interpretation guide (gain score calculation, proficiency decision logic), data collection template for tracking class-level learning gains"], "estimatedComplexity": "medium"}, {"title": "Automate Bilingual Figure Caption and Label Generation", "priority": "medium", "description": "Create script to extract all figure/diagram references from CoCu markdown files and auto-generate bilingual (English + Bahasa Malaysia) captions and labels with consistent terminology, ensuring publication-ready bilingual presentation.", "acceptanceCriteria": ["scripts/generate_bilingual_figure_captions.py scans content/IT-020-{3,4,5}/*.md for image file references and existing captions, produces output/Figure-Captions-Bilingual.json with structure: {figureId, imagePath, englishCaption, malayCaption, terminology: [term-pairs]}", "Script flags missing figures/captions for manual review; cross-references extracted Bahasa Malaysia terms against unified glossary to ensure consistency (use same translation across all 20 files)", "Output integrates with generate_docx.py to auto-render bilingual captions under all 50+ figures in final .docx with language tags for accessibility"], "estimatedComplexity": "small"}, {"title": "Classify All Learning Outcomes by Bloom's Taxonomy Cognitive Levels", "priority": "medium", "description": "Analyze all 200+ learning outcomes across 20 CoCu files and classify by Bloom's taxonomy level (Remember, Understand, Apply, Analyze, Evaluate, Create), identifying coverage gaps, pyramid alignment, and NOSS Knowledge-Performance split integrity.", "acceptanceCriteria": ["scripts/classify_bloom_outcomes.py scans all CoCu markdown files for Learning Outcome sections, produces output/Bloom-Classification-Report.json with per-CoCu breakdown: outcome statement, classified Bloom level, associated work activity, mapped assessment question/rubric", "Report includes: distribution histogram per CoCu and per level (e.g., 'L3 CoCu-1: 40% Remember, 35% Understand, 15% Apply, 10% Analyze, 0% Evaluate/Create'), identifies CoCu pyramid imbalances (e.g., <20% at Create/Evaluate levels too recall-heavy)", "Cross-validates against Knowledge (30%) / Performance (70%) split and flags misalignments; generates recommendations: 'CoCu-5 needs 4 additional Evaluate/Create outcomes for L5 management level' or 'Perfect progression: L3→70% Apply, L4→60% Analyze, L5→50% Evaluate'"], "estimatedComplexity": "small"}, {"title": "Generate Competency-Linked Instructor Feedback Response Templates", "priority": "low", "description": "Create bank of feedback response templates that instructors apply when assessing student work, each linked to specific rubric level (Novice/Developing/Proficient/Advanced), assessment criteria, and evidence of learning to support formative feedback consistency.", "acceptanceCriteria": ["scripts/generate_instructor_feedback_templates.py produces output/Instructor-Feedback-Response-Bank.docx organized by work activity with 4-level exemplars (≥60 work activities × 4 rubric levels = 240+ feedback samples)", "Each feedback exemplar: identifies specific evidence required for that rubric level, provides constructive next-step guidance aligned to learning outcome, references relevant assessment criteria and Bloom level, uses growth mindset language ('You've demonstrated X, next target Y' not 'You failed Z')", "Includes: feedback starter phrases by rubric level, template structure (evidence identified / progress noted / next steps / resources), guidance on linking feedback to assessor checklist"], "estimatedComplexity": "small"}]}
